<BaseLayout title="About | Kiden Scruton" description="Kiden Scruton: an aerospace engineering background with experience in hardware development, testing, fabrication, and team leadership.">
 <header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">About me</p><h1>I like making ideas work in the real world.</h1><p class="intro">My background is in aerospace engineering at the University of Hartford. My strongest interest is hardware: mechanical design, electronics, and the process of building and testing physical prototypes.</p></header>
 <div class="about-intro"><article class="prose"><h2>The hardware is what draws me in.</h2><p>The Brennan-inspired monorail is one of the projects I care most about. Bringing together flywheels, motors, mounts, sensing, and control made it an especially demanding build.</p><p>That is the kind of work I want this portfolio to show: making physical parts fit and behave together, then finding out where the model and the hardware disagree. Code and simulation are part of that process.</p><p>The monorail did not reach reliable stabilization. It still represents a substantial part of my work, from mechanical design and parts selection to wiring and Arduino control.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/brennan-gyro-monorail/">Explore the monorail build →</a></article><aside class="about-focus"><p class="eyebrow">What I want to work on</p><h2>Mechanisms and working prototypes.</h2><p>I’m interested in work that puts mechanical design, electronics, fabrication, and testing in the same process, with aerospace as an important part of my background.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">See the hardware projects →</a></aside></div>
 <section class="section-block" aria-labelledby="experience-title"><div class="section-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Experience in practice</p><h2 id="experience-title">Across the lab and the workbench.</h2></div></div><div class="about-experience">{experience.map(item=><article><p class="eyebrow">{item.url ? <a href={item.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{item.company} ↗</a> : item.company}</p><h3>{item.role}</h3><p>{item.description}</p><p>{experienceDetails[item.company as keyof typeof experienceDetails]}</p></article>)}</div></section>
 <section class="about-intro section-block" aria-labelledby="leadership-title"><article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Working with people</p><h2 id="leadership-title">Taking responsibility beyond my own part.</h2><p>The Connecticut Space Grant Consortium helped make two Wallops Flight Facility experiences possible for me: RockOn! first, then RockSat-C. After proving myself alongside Nick Krupa in RockOn!, I went on to co-lead the University of Hartford's first participation in RockSat-C. I helped coordinate technical work, timelines, procurement, and budgets alongside payload development. The 2025 mission completed launch, recovery, and data collection, and I was part of the launch team.</p><p>As founding president, I built the University of Hartford Kappa Sigma organization from nothing alongside two of my best friends. We developed recruitment and organizational processes, led events, and supported philanthropy. Earning our charter in January 2026 cemented the chapter’s status and made that shared effort a lasting part of the university.</p><p>Before university, my family and I built Scruton Brother’s Ice Cream from the ground up in Southern Pines, North Carolina. My brother and I ran daily operations for a couple of years before it closed in 2023. My own food allergies helped shape our dairy-free and gluten-free options; equipment problems and supply logistics taught me how to keep a business running. <a href="https://www.instagram.com/scrutonbrothersicecream/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See our family business on Instagram ↗</a></p></article><aside class="about-focus"><p class="eyebrow">Away from the desk</p><h2>Still making things.</h2><p>I enjoy model rocketry and airplane building, DIY electronics, custom computers, welding, and automotive maintenance. Outside the workshop, my interests include hiking, off-roading, and golf.</p></aside></section>
 <section class="section-block prose" aria-labelledby="community-title"><p class="eyebrow">Around the workshop</p><h2 id="community-title">Teams and shared interests</h2><p>My university activities include AIAA and founding involvement in AURORA, the Advanced Undergraduate Rocketry Operations and Research Association. I also attended a 3D-printing conference in Boston in spring 2026.</p><p>Personal interests feed the engineering side too: engines, simulation games, custom computers, model aircraft, rocketry, cars, fabrication, and repair work.</p><p><a href="/interests/">Explore the interests page and engine simulator →</a></p><p><a href="/resume/#leadership">Leadership, chapter founding, and the family business →</a></p></section>
 <div class="profile-cta"><div><h2>A closer look at my experience</h2><p>Roles, technical skills, selected projects, and recognition.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="/resume/">View my resume →</a></div>
</BaseLayout>


